{
 "about": "Title rules of the tech role set (engineering, design, legal), written by pipeline/roles_tech.py (do not edit by hand). Patterns are JavaScript regular expressions; use the 'i' flag. How to read a title: see 'how'.",
 "how": [
  "1. No role when the title matches 'not_the_job', or when the product set holds it: product.title_ok(title) and (product.family(title) is 'product_engineer' or the title does not match 'eng_word').",
  "2. The role is the first entry of 'families' whose 'patterns' match, or whose 'bare' pattern matches with the employer's say (see 'bare_titles'), and whose 'exclude' does not; an entry with 'engineering' true is also skipped when the title matches 'customer_facing', or matches 'hardware' and not 'software_word'.",
  "3. Ladder: 'legal' for counsel; 'bank' when the employer is in 'banks' or its industry in 'bank_industries' and a bank grade matches, or when the title matches 'bank_setoff' and not 'bank_setoff_not'; else 'engineering'.",
  "4. Level: the first grade of the ladder whose pattern matches; none: 'mid'.",
  "5. Entry mark: no mark when the title matches entry.title.not_for_them; the employer's row in entry.firms; 'grad' when the title matches entry.title.intern or entry.title.grad; on a level in entry.text.levels, 'grad' when the text matches entry.text.student and not entry.text.not_student."
 ],
